 ### `$URL()`
 
+### `appendQuery(input, query)`
+
+Appends values to the query section of the URL.
+
+Unlike `withQuery`, existing values are retained and new values are appended after them. Undefined values and empty arrays are ignored, while null and empty string values are encoded as empty query values. The `__proto__` and `constructor` keys are ignored to prevent prototype pollution.
+
+**Example:**
+
+```js
+appendQuery("/foo?tag=a&tag=b", { tag: ["c", "d"] });
+// "/foo?tag=a&tag=b&tag=c&tag=d"
+```
+
 ### `cleanDoubleSlashes(input)`
 
 Removes double slashes from the URL.
